  "at-0007": {
    "id": "at-0007",
    "kind": "lesson",
    "type": "business_policy",
    "topic": "idempotency-key",
    "title": "Money-moving functions take idempotency_key",
    "content": "Every function that moves money or changes a payment, credit or invoice balance must accept keyword-only `idempotency_key=None`, check `ledgerly.audit.events()` for an existing entry with that key before validating state, return the original result, and include the key in the audit entry (INC-204).",
    "scope": {
      "repo": "ledgerly",
      "observed_version": "1.0.0",
      "valid_from": "1.0.0",
      "valid_until": null,
      "files": [
        "ledgerly/adjustments.py"
      ]
    },
    "source": {
      "task_id": "E04",
      "first_pass": false,
      "review_comments": [
        "[team convention] Every operation that moves money or changes a payment, credit or invoice balance must accept an optional keyword-only `idempotency_key=None` (callers without a key keep working). Check the key first, before validating state: if an audit entry with the same key already exists (ledgerly.audit.events()), return the original result (for functions that return a record, the same record) without applying the operation again. Include `idempotency_key` in the audit entry you write. Introduced after the double-refund incident INC-204.",
        "[team convention] Support-initiated refunds and credits above 500.00 need a second approver (finance policy FIN-2026-03): accept an optional keyword-only `approved_by=None` (callers that do not need approval keep working). Amounts at or below 500.00 need no approval; above it, raise BillingError(\"approval_required\") when `approved_by` is missing."
      ],
      "references": [
        "INC-204"
      ],
      "proposed_by": "agent:distiller"
    },
    "evidence": [
      {
        "task_id": "E04",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "source": {
          "kind": "review_comment",
          "quote": "Every operation that moves money or changes a payment, credit or invoice balance must accept an optional keyword-only `idempotency_key=None`",
          "references": [
            "INC-204"
          ],
          "comment": "[team convention] Every operation that moves money or changes a payment, credit or invoice balance must accept an optional keyword-only `idempotency_key=None` (callers without a key keep working). Check the key first, before validating state: if an audit entry with the same key already exists (ledgerly.audit.events()), return the original result (for functions that return a record, the same record) without applying the operation again. Include `idempotency_key` in the audit entry you write. Introduced after the double-refund incident INC-204."
        },
        "applied": {
          "kind": "code",
          "change": "added",
          "file": "ledgerly/adjustments.py",
          "line": "def refund(payment, amount, at, *, idempotency_key=None, approved_by=None):",
